[38;5;252m[1m## The one real bug found[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation was functionally correct for all finite inputs but produced the wrong [1mNaN payload[22m. [38;5;10mhsv_to_rgb[0m computes three products of the form [38;5;10mv * (1 - …)[0m. On x86, [38;5;10mmulss src1, src2[0m forwards [38;5;10msrc1[0m's NaN when both operands are NaN, and gcc emits these multiplications with the operands [3mswapped relative to the C source[23m — the [38;5;10m(1 - …)[0m subexpression lands in the destination register, not [38;5;10mv[0m. LLVM chose the opposite order, so whenever both [38;5;10mv[0m and the other operand were NaN, Rust returned [38;5;10mv[0m's payload where C returned the other one.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I read the operand order off [38;5;10mobjdump -d[0m of the C object and encoded it explicitly in [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m via [38;5;10msse_mul[0m/[38;5;10msse_sub[0m/[38;5;10msse_div[0m helpers that implement the Intel NaN-forwarding rule (forward [38;5;10msrc1[0m if NaN, else [38;5;10msrc2[0m, quietening signalling NaNs by setting mantissa bit 22). This pins the behaviour regardless of what LLVM does with the commutative operations. The pre-existing [38;5;10mc_floor_to_int[0m emulation of [38;5;10m(int)floorf(h)[0m — [38;5;10mcvttss2si[0m yields [38;5;10mINT_MIN[0m for NaN and out-of-range values rather than saturating — was already correct and is confirmed by tests.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Test harness[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mtranslation/tests/common/mod.rs[0m loads both shared objects with [38;5;10mlibloading[0m and resolves [38;5;10mhsv_to_rgb[0m from each; the Rust side is never called directly, so the [38;5;10m#[no_mangle][0m wrapper is exercised. Two details worth knowing:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- The C library's name is derived from the containing directory name by CMake, so the harness globs [38;5;10mc_src/build/lib*.so[0m rather than hardcoding it.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mcargo test[0m does [1mnot[22m build or refresh [38;5;10mcdylib[0m artifacts. An early run silently tested a stale [38;5;10m.so[0m left in [38;5;10mtarget/debug/deps/[0m by a prior [38;5;10mcargo build[0m and reported the same failures after I'd already fixed them. The harness now always rebuilds the library into a separate target directory (the outer [38;5;10mcargo test[0m holds the lock on the main one), so the artifact under test always matches the sources.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Outputs are compared as raw [38;5;10mu32[0m bit patterns so NaN payloads and signed zeros are exact, and the 3-float output window is surrounded by [38;5;10m0xDEADBEEF[0m guards to catch out-of-bounds writes.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
